    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "\\begin{align*}\n & \\mathbf{What\\,is\\,the\\,remainder\\,when\\,the\\,sum\\,of\\,the\\,first\\,five\\,primes\\,is\\,divided\\,by\\,the\\,\n  sixth\\,prime?} \\\\\\frac{2+3+5+7+11}{13}&=\\,\\frac{28}{13}\\,\\,\\,\\times\\,\\underbrace{4}_{\\text{Remainder=28-13}}\\,\\\\&\\underline{\\phantom{\\frac{28}{13}}}\\qquad\\times\\qquad\\,& \\boxed{2}\\\\&\\qquad\\qquad\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\text{Remainder =2}\\end{align*}\nThe answer is 2\n\nKey Takeaways: An algorithm can be developed in an intuitive manner when solving a problem. You are given $6$ unique cookies. To determine the probability that each cookie is eaten in each order, determine the number of ways in which each cookie is chosen at least once. Then divide this number by the total number of ways.",
