    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime, we first need to identify these primes:\n\n1. The first prime number is \\(2\\).\n2. The second prime number is \\(3\\).\n3. The third prime number is \\(5\\).\n4. The fourth prime number is \\(7\\).\n5. The fifth prime number is \\(11\\).\n6. The sixth prime number is \\(13\\).\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of the first five prime numbers:\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11\n\\]\n\nWe will add these numbers step by step:\n\n\\[\n2 + 3 = 5\n\\]\n\\[\n5 + 5 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n10 + 7 = 17\n\\]\n\\[\n17 + 11 = 28\n\\]\n\nSo, the sum of the first five prime numbers is \\(28\\).\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when \\(28\\) is divided by the sixth prime number, which is \\(13\\).\n\nWe perform the division of \\(28\\) by \\(13\\):\n\\[\n28 \\div 13 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 2\n\\]\n\nThis means that \\(28 = 13 \\times 2 + 2\\). Here, the remainder is \\(2\\).\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
